          "english": "If you think life is wonderful and expect it to stay that way, then you may have a good chance of living to a ripe old age, at least that is what the findings of a new study suggest. That study found that participants who reported the highest levels of optimism were far more likely to live to age 85 or __(26)__ . This was compared to those participants who reported the lowest levels of optimism. It is __(27)__ that the findings held even after the researchers considered factors that could __(28)__ the link, including whether participants had health conditions such as heart disease or cancer, or whether they experienced depression. The results add to a growing body of evidence that certain psychological factors may predict a longer life __(29)__ . For example, previous studies have found that more optimistic people have a lower risk of developing chronic diseases, and a lower risk of __(30)__ death. However, the new study appears to be the first to __(31)__ look at the relationship between optimism and longevity. The researchers __(32)__ that the link found in the new study was not as strong when they factored in the effects of certain health behaviors, including exercise levels, sleep habits and diet. This suggests that these behaviors may, at least in part, explain the link. In other words, optimism may __(33)__ good habits that bolster health. It is also important to note that the study found only a __(34)__ , as researchers did not prove for certain that optimism leads to a longer life. However, if the findings are true, they suggest that optimism could serve as a psychological __(35)__ that promotes health and a longer life.",
          "chinese": "如果你认为生活是美好的，并期望它能保持这种状态，那么你很有可能会活到高寿，至少一项新研究的结果是这样提示的。该研究发现，报告乐观程度最高的受试者活到85岁及以上的可能性要高得多。这是与那些报告乐观程度最低的受试者相比而言的。值得注意的是，即使研究人员考虑了可能影响这种联系的因素，包括受试者是否患有心脏病或癌症等健康状况，或者是否经历过抑郁，这一结论依然成立。这些结果增添了越来越多的证据，表明某些心理因素可能会预测更长的寿命。例如，先前的研究发现，更为乐观的人患慢性病的风险较低，早逝的风险也较低。然而，这项新研究似乎是第一项专门探讨乐观与长寿之间关系的研究。研究人员承认，当他们将某些健康行为的影响（包括运动水平、睡眠习惯和饮食）纳入考量时，新研究中发现的这种联系就没有那么强烈了。这表明，这些行为可能至少在一定程度上解释了这种联系。换句话说，乐观可能会培养增进健康的良好习惯。同样重要的是要注意，该研究仅发现了一种相关性，因为研究人员并没有确切证明乐观会导致更长的寿命。然而，如果这些发现属实，它们表明乐观可以作为一种促进健康和长寿的心理特质。",
